From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel Arto <manuelartociao@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:20:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix(daisugi): commit to signature lengths in the
 EIP-8141 signature hash

ethereum/EIPs#12502 replaces the signature bytes of empty-msg entries with
their length in compute_sig_hash, and Nethermind feature/eip8288-lean follows it
since ad9f8ca650. A zero data_hash dependency resolves to that hash, so the
Daisugi block hash check must use the same rule.

The unit vectors are recomputed against Nethermind b0e83c01bf with the current
frame transaction layout. Block 447 of a local devnet on that build adds a
proof-bearing block with zero data_hash dependencies; the earlier block 2503
fixture now documents that a block hashed under the old rule no longer
reproduces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
